# What the xenithos-desktop package needs: the desktop itself (XFCE), what its look is made of,
# and the tools its session, Settings and updates use. An update that adds a line here brings
# that package to every installed PC.

## The desktop
xfce4-session
xfwm4
xfce4-panel
xfdesktop4
xfce4-settings
xfconf
thunar
thunar-volman
thunar-archive-plugin
gvfs
gvfs-backends
tumbler
xfce4-terminal
xfce4-whiskermenu-plugin
xfce4-pulseaudio-plugin
xfce4-notifyd
xfce4-power-manager
xfce4-power-manager-plugins
network-manager-gnome
mate-polkit
xdg-utils
xdg-user-dirs
at-spi2-core
libglib2.0-bin
dconf-gsettings-backend
gsettings-desktop-schemas

## Its look
papirus-icon-theme
gtk-update-icon-cache
adwaita-icon-theme
hicolor-icon-theme
librsvg2-common
fonts-inter
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-noto-color-emoji
# The world's other writing (Chinese, Japanese and Korean, then the rest), so web pages and file
# names in them show as letters and not as empty boxes.
fonts-noto-cjk
fonts-noto-core
plymouth
plymouth-label
qt5-gtk-platformtheme
qt6-gtk-platformtheme

